<title>USA: Cultor takes stake in Aquasearch.</title>
<headline>Cultor takes stake in Aquasearch.</headline>
<dateline>KAILUA-KONA, Hawaii 1996-10-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marine bioscience company Aquasearch Inc said Cultor Ltd, a multi-billion-dollar Finnish food conglomerate and worldwide producer of animal feeds, bought 400,000 shares of Aquasearch's common stock.</p>
<p>The deal was struck at $0.50 per share, pursuant to terms of a May 1996 stock subscription agreement previously announced between the two companies.</p>
</text>
